<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel"> 
      <p xml:id="Aink168-kilavi">
       kātaṟparattaiyaiviṭṭu maṟṟoruttiyuṭaṉ oḻukāniṉṟa talaimakaṉ vāyilvēṇṭi viṭuttuḻi vāyiṉērtalvēṇṭi niṉkaṇ pacantaṉakāṇeṉṟu mukampuku tōḻikkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
         Spoken by the heroine to the confidante who asked for a favour [on his behalf], saying 'your eyes have turned pale', the hero who was with another lady [after] having left the other beloved woman, desiring a mediator [= the heroine; and] sending [her] ahead, wished [for the heroine] to agree [to let him] enter. </p>
  </div>  
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink169">
<l>peruṅkaṭaṟ karaiyatu ciṟuveṇ kākkai</l>
<l>poṉṉiṇar ñāḻaṉ muṇaiyiṟ potiyaviḻ</l>
<l>puṉṉaiyam pūñciṉaic cēkkun tuṟaiva</l>
<l>ṉeñcat tuṇmai yaṟintu</l>
<l>meṉceyap pacakkun tōḻiyeṉ kaṇṇē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>Despite knowing the truth of [my] heart [about]</l>
        <l>The man of the shore in which the small white crow</l>
        <l>Of the seashore rests [in] the flowering branches of the Puṉṉai tree</l>
        <l>[On which] buds open, if it dislikes the Ñāḻal tree [with] golden clusters,</l>
        <l>For what [reason] do my eyes become pallid, oh friend?</l>
              </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
